@page
@model countrybitweb.Pages.RevolutionIdeasModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Revolution Ideas";
}

<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
<a style="font-size:20px; color:darkgreen;" href="https://apps.microsoft.com/detail/9mw7vxj5l36r?hl=en-US&gl=US">See in the Microsoft Store</a>

<h3>Experiment with modelling different institutions</h3>
<p>
    Our low code Corona fabric lets you model different institutions and see how they work.  
    You can model a country, a business, a school, or any other kind of institution.  We come with preloaded schemas,
    but invite you to change and tinker with as you will.  Note that all of our products actually have this capability.
</p>

<h3>Handcrafted, Small and Fast</h3>
<p>
    Revolution Ideas was written in powerful C++ directly to the Windows operating
    system. It can run on just about any PC.
</p>

<h3>Where to Buy</h3>
<p>
    Revolution Ideas is at the Microsoft Store.
</p>

<h3>About the Author</h3>
<p>
    Revolution Ideas was written by Todd Bandrowsky, of Bowling Green, KY.
</p>

